{"title":"Understanding photosynthesis and its three key inputs","key_idea":"Plants make their own food using sunlight, water, and carbon dioxide; they need all three inputs to survive and grow.","method":["Name the three things a plant needs: sunlight from the sun, water from the soil, and carbon dioxide from the air.","Remember that the plant uses these three ingredients like a chef uses ingredients in a kitchen.","Know that the plant makes glucose (food) to grow, and releases oxygen as a helpful byproduct.","Think about what happens if any one ingredient is missing — the plant cannot make food and will weaken."],"worked_example":{"problem":"A plant sits on a sunny windowsill with water in the soil and fresh air around it. What does the plant make, and what does it release?","steps":["The plant has sunlight from the window, water from the soil, and air around it.","The plant combines these three inputs using its leaves.","The plant makes glucose (food) to use for growing and energy.","The plant releases oxygen into the air as a byproduct."],"answer":"The plant makes glucose and releases oxygen."},"key_terms":[{"term":"photosynthesis","meaning":"the process where plants use sunlight, water, and carbon dioxide to make food"},{"term":"glucose","meaning":"the food (sugar) that the plant makes and uses to grow"},{"term":"byproduct","meaning":"something extra that is made when the main job is done"}],"common_mistakes":["Thinking plants get food from the soil — they make their own food using sunlight and water.","Forgetting that plants need all three inputs: if even one is missing, photosynthesis cannot happen."],"remember":"No sunlight, water, or air means no food and no survival for the plant.","quick_check":[{"q":"What are the three inputs a plant needs to make food?","a":"Sunlight, water, and carbon dioxide."},{"q":"If a plant is kept in a dark room with water and air, what will happen to it?","a":"It cannot make food because it has no sunlight, so it will weaken and may die."}],"tell_your_child":"Think of your plant as a little chef who needs three things to cook: sunshine for energy, water from the ground, and fresh air. Without all three, the plant cannot cook its own meal and grow strong."}
```
